---
source: crates/safix/src/reporter.rs
expression: render_plain(&refusal)
---
safix: 'bo' is not you, and this writes a private key into your own
identity file.

An age identity is custody: everything encrypted to its public half is
readable by whoever holds this private half. Minting one for another
person on your machine means you hold their key, which is the opposite of
the independent custody this package is built on. They should run this
themselves and hand you the public half.

If you have decided otherwise anyway, say so:

    safix keygen --for-someone-else bo
